# LAN Chat — ESP32 Web Chat Server

A self-hosted LAN chat server running entirely on an ESP32. No internet, no cloud, no external server — just a single ESP32 on your local network serving a full-featured group chat to any browser on the same WiFi.

![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/platform-ESP32-blue)
![Framework](https://img.shields.io/badge/framework-Arduino-teal)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)

---

 Features

- Zero-install client — open a browser, enter a name, chat. No app to install.
- Multiple rooms — General, Tech, Random (easy to extend).
- Direct messages — click any sender's name to send a DM.
- Admin mode — login with a password to unlock moderation tools:
  - View all connected users (IP, room, admin flag)
  - Remove / ban users by IP
  - Delete any message
  - View a rolling activity log
- File & image sharing — up to 50 KB per file, inline images, download links.
- Message editing — your own messages can be edited after sending.
- Typing indicator — see who is typing in real time.
- Persistence — chat history survives reboots via LittleFS.
- Sound & notifications — in-browser beep on new messages, optional desktop notifications.
- Comprehensive serial logging — every HTTP request, login attempt, filesystem operation, and WiFi event is logged with a `[TAG]` prefix for easy debugging.

