 Quick Start

1. Clone the repository

bash
git clone https://github.com/maran126/LAN-CHATBOX
cd esp32-lan-chat


2. Configure WiFi

Open the sketch and edit the configuration block at the top:

cpp
const char* ssid       = "YOUR_WIFI";
const char* password   = "YOUR_WIFI_PASSWORD";
const char* ADMIN_PASS = "admin123";


> Note: `ADMIN_PASS` is the password a user types into the login screen to become admin. Change it before deploying.

### 3. Add the partition table

Create a file named `partitions.csv` in the project root:

```csv
# Name,   Type, SubType, Offset,   Size,     Flags
nvs,      data, nvs,     0x9000,   0x5000,
otadata,  data, ota,     0xE000,   0x2000,
app0,     app,  ota_0,   0x10000,  0x140000,
app1,     app,  ota_1,   0x150000, 0x140000,
spiffs,   data, spiffs,  0x290000, 0x160000,
coredump, data, coredump,0x3F0000, 0x10000,
```

This reserves a 1.4 MB LittleFS partition for chat history. The sketch mounts it as `spiffs`.

4. Set the filesystem label in the sketch

The label must match the partition table:

```cpp
#define FS_PARTITION_LABEL "spiffs"
```

5. Flash (PlatformIO — recommended)

Add to `platformio.ini`:

```ini
[env:esp32dev]
platform = espressif32
board = esp32dev
framework = arduino
board_build.partitions = partitions.csv
board_build.filesystem = littlefs
monitor_speed = 115200
```

Flash in this order — the erase step is required the first time because the default partition table has no `spiffs` partition:

```bash
pio run -t erase
pio run -t upload
pio run -t uploadfs
pio device monitor
```

6. Flash (Arduino IDE)

1. Set Tools → Board to your ESP32 model.
2. Select a partition scheme that includes SPIFFS/LittleFS (e.g. *"Default 4MB with spiffs"*).
3. Upload the sketch.
4. Open Tools → ESP32 Sketch Data Upload to upload the filesystem image (requires the `arduino-esp32fs-plugin`).

7. Connect

Open the serial monitor at 115200 baud. You should see:

```
[    1509] [BOOT] === starting ===
[    1510] [FS] Mounting 'spiffs' @ 0x290000 size 0x160000
[    1511] [FS] OK  total=1441792 used=0
[    1561] [WIFI] connecting to 'YOUR_WIFI'
..........
[    8165] [WIFI] connected  IP=192.168.1.42  RSSI=-55 dBm  channel=6
[    8167] [BOOT] Chat Server: http://192.168.1.42
```

Open `http://192.168.1.42` in any browser on the same network.

