Usage

As a client

1. Open the web page.
2. Enter a username.
3. Leave the password field empty.
4. Click Join.

You can now chat in the selected room, switch rooms, send files, and DM other users by clicking their name.

As an admin

1. Enter a username.
2. Enter the admin password (`admin123` by default).
3. Click Join.

The admin panel appears with the user list and activity log. Only one admin can be active at a time — the slot is released when the ESP32 reboots.

 Moderation actions

| Action                | How                                               | 
|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| Delete a message      | Hover the message → click `x` (admin only)        |
| Edit your own message | Hover the message → click `Edit`                  |
| Remove a user         | Admin panel → click **Remove** next to their name |
| Ban a user            | Removing a user also bans their IP until reboot   |

---

 Architecture

```
Browser (any device on LAN)
        │  HTTP  (GET requests, JSON responses)
        ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ESP32                               │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ WebServer (port 80)            │  │
│  │  /             → HTML UI       │  │
│  │  /login        → auth          │  │
│  │  /send         → post message  │  │
│  │  /sendfile     → post file     │  │
│  │  /edit         → edit message  │  │
│  │  /typing       → typing signal │  │
│  │  /msgs         → message feed  │  │
│  │  /count        → online count  │  │
│  │  /users        → admin: users  │  │
│  │  /activity     → admin: log    │  │
│  │  /remove       → admin: ban    │  │
│  │  /delmsg       → admin: del    │  │
│  └──────────────┬─────────────────┘  │
│                 │                    │
│  ┌──────────────▼─────────────────┐  │
│  │ In-RAM ring buffers            │  │
│  │  users[MAX_USERS]              │  │
│  │  messages[MAX_MESSAGES]        │  │
│  │  activities[MAX_ACTIVITIES]    │  │
│  │  banned[MAX_BANNED]            │  │
│  └──────────────┬─────────────────┘  │
│                 │                    │
│  ┌──────────────▼─────────────────┐  │
│  │ LittleFS (spiffs partition)    │  │
│  │  /chat.json                    │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────┘  │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Design notes:

- Polling, not WebSockets — simpler, works on any ESP32 core, no handshake issues. The browser polls `/msgs` every 1 s and `/count` every 2 s.
- Ring buffers in RAM — bounded memory, old messages dropped when full (`MAX_MESSAGES` = 50).
- Persistence to LittleFS on every message — survives reboot.
- Users and bans are RAM-only — cleared on reboot, so a power cycle resets the ban list and frees the admin slot.

