 Serial Log Tags

Every action is logged with a short tag so you can `grep` the monitor:

| Tag          | Meaning                                               |
|--------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| `[BOOT]`     | Startup phase                                         |
| `[FS]`       | Filesystem mount, read, write                         |
| `[WIFI]`     | Connect, reconnect, heartbeat (every 15 s)            |
| `[HTTP]`     | Every incoming request (method, path, client IP)      |
| `[LOGIN]`    | Login attempt details                                 |
| `[SEND]`     | Message send                                          |
| `[MSG]`      | Message stored                                        |
| `[FILE]`     | File upload                                           |
| `[EDIT]`     | Message edit                                          |
| `[DEL]`      | Message delete                                        |
| `[TYPING]`   | Typing indicator                                      |
| `[MSGS]`     | Messages feed polled                                  |
| `[USERS]`    | Admin user list requested                             |
| `[ACTIVITY]` | Admin activity log requested                          |
| `[REMOVE]`   | User removed                                          |
| `[BAN]`      | IP added to ban list                                  |
| `[ACT]`      | Activity log entry written                            |
| `[404]`      | Unknown route                                         |

Example:

```
[   35174] [HTTP] GET / from 10.211.251.130
[   35175] [HTTP] served index (12473 bytes)
[   36815] [HTTP] GET /login from 10.211.251.130
[   36816] [LOGIN] name='Alice' passLen=0 room='General' ip=10.211.251.130 users=0
[   36818] [LOGIN] OK  name='Alice' admin=0 users=1
[   36819] [ACT] Alice joined General
```

